  "title": "Builder-family detection and diff-anchored review posting",
  "summary": "Two coupled changes to `osf review`. First, builder-family detection now scans every word (and every `/`-separated part of a word) of a `Code-Generator:` trailer's model name against a single shared `agents::MODEL_FAMILIES` table, so vendor-first names like `Anthropic Claude Code claude-sonnet-5-5` resolve to `anthropic`; a name whose words point at two families is `unknown`, and an unknown builder family now fails the run closed (could-not-run, exit 2) instead of running the whole roster. Second, review posting fetches the pull request's diff via `gh pr diff`, parses the right-side hunk ranges, and only emits inline comments for findings that land on commentable lines — everything else moves into the review body under \"Findings outside the diff\", avoiding GitHub's HTTP 422 for out-of-diff inline comments.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
